,["hs","sh"],["at","West's heart opening lead is taken by South with the @HA. "],["pg",""],["ls","Sh"],["pc","hh6h"],["pg",""],["hs","nssses"],["at","East's 1NT opening marks him with most of the outstanding high cards so it looks like South should be able to hold his losers to 1 spade "],["pg",""],["ls","nssses"],["hs","ncscec"],["at","and 2 clubs. "],["pg",""],["ls","ncscec"],["hs","nssses"],["nt","The main danger to the contract is that East might have all 4 outstanding spades. In this case, South can prevent East from winning 2 trump tricks by starting the suit with a low card to dummy's @SJ. "],["pg",""],["ls","nssses"],["pc","s"],["hs","wh"],["at","West's discard confirms the 4-0 trump break "],["pg",""],["ls","wh"],["pc","H"],["hs","nses"],["at","and East takes dummy's @SJ with the @SA. "],["pg",""],["ls","nses"],["pc","sjsa"],["pg",""],["hs","eh"],["at","East returns a heart. "],["pg",""],["ls","eh"],["pc","hk"],["hs","ss"],["nt","It would be a mistake for South to ruff this trick. "],["pg",""],["ls","ss"],["pc","shh"],["pg",""],["hs","ndsd"],["at","The best South could then do is cross to the dummy in diamonds "],["pg",""],["ls","ndsd"],["pc","dddd"],["pg",""],["hs","ssns"],["at","in order to lead a second round of trump toward the closed hand. "],["pg",""],["ls","nsss"],["pc","s"],["hs","esss"],["at","East would insert the @S8 to force an honor from South. "],["pg",""],["ls","esss"],["pc","s8skh"],["pg",""],["hs","ndsd"],["at","South would continue with another diamond to the dummy "],["pg",""],["ls","ndsd"],["pc","dddd"],["pg",""],["hs","nssses"],["at","to finesse again in trump. "],["pg",""],["ls","nssses"],["pc","sssh"],["pg",""],["hs","sses"],["nt","South is now in trouble. If he draws East's last trump "],["pg",""],["ls","sses"],["pc","shss"],["pg",""],["hs","ndsd"],["at","and crosses to the dummy in diamonds "],["pg",""],["ls","ndsd"],["pc","dddc"],["pg",""],["hs","ncscec"],["at","in order to play a club toward his @CK, East will take the @CA "],["pg",""],["ls","ecncsc"],["pc","ccacc"],["pg",""],["hs","eh"],["at","and cash heart tricks to defeat the contract. "],["pg",""],["ls","eh"],["up","12"],["hs","scesns"],["at","If South tries to set up a club trick while a trump remains outstanding (so that the dummy's last trump can be used to ruff the next round of hearts) "],["pg",""],["ls","nssc"],["hs","ndsd"],["at","the contract will fail on the actual layout as East will be able to ruff the third round of diamonds. "],["pg",""],["ls","ndsdes"],["up","19"],["hs","sc"],["nt","South can maintain trump control by discarding a club loser on the second round of hearts. "],["pg",""],["ls","sc"],["pc","chh"],["pg",""],["hs","ehns"],["at","If East continues hearts South can take the ruff in the dummy and maintain trump control. "],["pg",""],["ls","ehns"],["hs","ednd"],["at","If instead East defends passively by returning a diamond, South wins in the dummy "],["pg",""],["ls","ednd"],["pc","dddd"],["pg",""],["hs","nssses"],["at","in order to play a trump through East. "],["pg",""],["ls","nsesss"],["pc","ss8skh"],["pg",""],["hs","ndsd"],["at","South can return to the dummy in diamonds, "],["pg",""],["ls","ndsd"],["pc","dddd"],["pg",""],["hs","nssses"],["at","finesse against East's @S10, "],["pg",""],["ls","nssses"],["pc","sssh"],["pg",""],["hs","sses"],["at","and draw the last trump. "],["pg",""],["ls","sses"],["pc","sqhss"],["pg",""],["hs","ndsd"],["nt","Now that East is out of trump it is safe to cross to the dummy a third time in diamonds. "],["pg",""],["ls","ndsd"],["pc","dddc"],["pg",""],["hs","ncscec"],["at","South continues with a club toward the @CK which East takes with the @CA. "],["pg",""],["ls","ecscnc"],["pc","ccacc"],["pg",""],["hs","ehss"],["at","South has a trump remaining to handle a force from East. "],["pg",""],["ls","ehss"],["pc","hqsdc"],["pg",""],["hs","scsd"],["at","South will win the last 2 tricks with his remaining diamond and the @CK and make the contract."],["",""]]}}